no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-catalog: build the scope ring, cached per-scope note snapshots, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the note tree, and the generated-note contract the panel reads.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared memory-note mutation engine[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-writes[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-writes: add a CLI-free create/update/delete engine for memory [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notes with pure validation, atomic writes, a stale-write guard, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]delete backups.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ace.keymaps.memory binding scope[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]panel-keymaps[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel-keymaps: register the panel-scoped keymap dataclass, defaults, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]config schema, binding builders, and app help sections.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Memory panel shell, note tree, filter, and scope switching[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]panel-shell[dim] · [dim][/dim]after memory-catalog, panel-keymaps[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel-shell: build the modal, the nested note rail, the note card, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]filtering, scope cycling and picking, empty/error states, and passive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]open/copy actions.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Parent and child link travel[/bold #D7AFFF]                                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]panel-links[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel-shell[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel-links: add the numbered PARENT/CHILDREN chips, chip cursor, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]numbered follow, and the bounded breadcrumb trail with back travel.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Add, edit, delete, and publish surfaces[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]panel-mutations[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel-shell, memory-writes[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel-mutations: wire the add/edit forms, the delete confirmation, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tracked-proc writes, and the sase memory init publish flow with its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unpublished state.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prompt gm and Ctrl+G m entry point[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]prompt-entry[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel-shell[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prompt-entry: claim the prompt g-prefix m continuation, post the request[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]message, open the panel seeded from the memory reference under the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cursor, and restore focus.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation, visual snapshots, and full verification[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-panel-verification[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel-links, panel-mutations, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]prompt-entry[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-panel-verification: document the panel and its keymap scope, add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PNG snapshot goldens, and run the exhaustive verification lanes.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-qt","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__